# shellcheck shell=bash disable=SC2034
# GNOME Remote Desktop (system / headless login) — sourced by
# /usr/local/sbin/appbox-configure-gnome-rdp.sh at boot and after install.
#
# RDP_PORT: TCP port for Windows Remote Desktop (mstsc). Override in production
# (e.g. cloud-init) to match your port mapping.
RDP_PORT=3389

# Optional: fixed credentials for the *first* RDP handshake (GDM login screen).
# If unset, a random password is generated once and stored in
# /etc/gnome-remote-desktop/rdp-secret (mode 0600).
GRD_RDP_USERNAME='appbox'
# GRD_RDP_PASSWORD=

# --- TLS (critical for Windows mstsc) ---
# If the name or IP you type in "Computer" is not in the certificate SAN, Windows
# often disconnects within seconds with no login UI (e.g. internal error / 0x4).
# RDP_TLS_CN: Common Name (defaults to `hostname -f`).
# RDP_TLS_EXTRA_SAN: extra comma-separated entries, e.g.
#   DNS:vm.public.example.com,IP:203.0.113.10
# RDP_TLS_REGEN=1: force new key+cert on next run, then remove this line.
# RDP_TLS_CN=vm.public.example.com
# RDP_TLS_EXTRA_SAN=DNS:vm.public.example.com,IP:203.0.113.10
# RDP_TLS_REGEN=1
